{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b269525d57d3bda082d2d7df17a1f0743db10f834214585058992063b1e92a11","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / attestation / code-drift invalidation","key_entities":["dependency_hashes","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","sign_plan_review","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","material_fingerprint","p9_file_impact_coverage","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py","ctx.children","orchestrator.assemble_context","docs/plan-review-gate.md","docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md"],"problem_keywords":["container plan-review","drift invalidation","file_impact inheritance","attestation scope","poison rule","whole-HEAD fallback"],"propositions":["Container tickets with no declared file_impact fall back to whole-HEAD invalidation, causing re-reviews on every unrelated commit; they should instead inherit their direct children's file_impact union to narrow the dependency set.","A poison rule prevents inheritance when any non-closed direct child declares empty file_impact, preserving fail-closed semantics and avoiding silent staleness beyond one level of the ticket hierarchy.","Closed children do not contribute files or poison the inherited union, and child file_impact edits invalidate the container attestation via material fingerprint drift.","The P9 determinism floor should surface an advisory (never blocking) naming children with empty file_impact when inheritance is poisoned, so authors understand why the container remains on whole-HEAD invalidation."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787332930852079001,"uuid":"b11